<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115334" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαμμᾰκόσιοι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αι</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sand-hundred,</i> Com. word formed from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμμος</span> after the analogy of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακόσιοι, τριακόσιοι,</span> etc., to denote
			a countless multitude, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. θεαταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					286
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαμμοκ-</span>
			v. l. ap.<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.671a
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνόματα ψ.</span>
			<i>grandiloquent</i> terms, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.230d
			</span></i>.—So the exaggerated form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαμμᾰκοσιογάργᾰροι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αι</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				3
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαμμοκ-</span>
			): cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάργαρα.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
